---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { store } from '../data/store';
import { url } from '../lib/shop';
---
<Layout title="Terms" description={`The terms for buying from ${store.name}.`}>
	<div class="wrap page-head">
		<h1>Terms of sale</h1>
		<p>Sample terms for a theme demo. Replace them with your own before you sell anything; they are not legal advice.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="wrap prose">
		<h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
		<p>{store.name}, {store.location}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${store.email}`}>{store.email}</a>.</p>
		<h2>Prices and payment</h2>
		<p>Prices are shown in US dollars and exclude shipping and any sales tax or VAT, which are added on the Stripe checkout page before you pay. Payment is taken by Stripe when you place the order. If a price on this site is wrong, we will tell you before shipping and offer a refund.</p>
		<h2>Your order</h2>
		<p>Your order is accepted when Stripe confirms the payment and sends your receipt. If we cannot fulfil it, for example because an item sold out at the same moment, we refund you in full within 5 working days.</p>
		<h2>Delivery, returns and refunds</h2>
		<p>See <a href={url('/shipping/')}>shipping and returns</a>. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under the consumer law of your country.</p>
		<h2>Handmade goods</h2>
		<p>Our notebooks and trays are made by hand. Small differences in thread tension, grain and color between items are normal and are not defects.</p>
		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>We may update these terms. The version on this page when you place an order is the one that applies to it.</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
